WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.601
Mary ran so fast that she was out of breath when she reached her rooms.

2
00:00:07.602 --> 00:00:14.361
Martha was waiting. "You're late," she told Mary. "Where have you been?"

3
00:00:14.362 --> 00:00:18.317
"I've seen Dickon!" Mary exclaimed.

4
00:00:18.318 --> 00:00:23.639
Martha wanted to know all about the garden tools and seeds that he had brought.

5
00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:27.217
"Did you ask someone where you might plant the seeds?"

6
00:00:27.218 --> 00:00:31.617
Mary was afraid to reveal anything about the secret garden.

7
00:00:31.618 --> 00:00:36.809
"I haven't asked anybody yet," she said hesitantly.

8
00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:42.557
"Well, I wouldn't ask the head gardener, Mr. Roach. He's a bit haughty.

9
00:00:42.558 --> 00:00:46.631
I'd ask Ben Weatherstaff, who's kinder than he looks.

10
00:00:46.632 --> 00:00:52.567
Mr. Craven lets him do what he likes because he was here when Mrs. Craven was alive.

11
00:00:52.568 --> 00:00:56.246
He used to make her laugh, and she liked him.

12
00:00:56.247 --> 00:00:59.933
Perhaps he'd find you a corner somewhere."

13
00:00:59.934 --> 00:01:01.977
Mary ate lunch quickly.

14
00:01:01.978 --> 00:01:06.142
She was eager to go back to working in the secret garden with Dickon.

15
00:01:06.143 --> 00:01:11.653
She hopped up from the table and was about to run outside, when Martha stopped her.

16
00:01:11.654 --> 00:01:13.746
"I've got something to tell you.

17
00:01:13.747 --> 00:01:19.207
Mr. Craven came back this morning, and he wants to see you."

18
00:01:19.208 --> 00:01:25.627
Mary turned pale. "Oh, why? He didn't want to see me when I first came."

19
00:01:25.628 --> 00:01:32.405
"Mrs. Medlock says it's because Mother met him when she was walking to Thwaite village," said Martha.

20
00:01:32.406 --> 00:01:39.484
"She'd never spoken to him before, but Mrs. Craven had been to our cottage two or three times.

21
00:01:39.485 --> 00:01:45.674
I don't know what Mother said to him, but he wants to see you before he goes away again tomorrow."

22
00:01:45.675 --> 00:01:50.588
"Oh!" cried Mary. "I'm so glad he's going away again."

23
00:01:50.589 --> 00:01:54.054
"He may not come back until autumn or winter.

24
00:01:54.055 --> 00:01:58.432
He's going to be traveling to several different places."

25
00:01:58.433 --> 00:02:05.706
If Mr. Craven didn't come back until autumn or winter, there would be time to watch the secret garden come alive.

26
00:02:05.707 --> 00:02:12.528
"Even if he finds out then and takes it away from me," Mary thought, "I will at least have had that much."

27
00:02:12.529 --> 00:02:17.855
Suddenly the door opened, and Mrs. Medlock stepped into the room.

28
00:02:17.856 --> 00:02:23.151
"Go brush your hair, and get into your best dress," she said to Mary.

29
00:02:23.152 --> 00:02:27.077
"Mr. Craven sent me to bring you to his study."

30
00:02:27.078 --> 00:02:34.060
Mary's heart began to thump, and she felt herself changing into a stiff, plain child again.

31
00:02:34.061 --> 00:02:37.470
She said nothing while Martha helped her get dressed.

32
00:02:37.471 --> 00:02:41.738
She followed Mrs. Medlock silently down the corridors.

33
00:02:41.739 --> 00:02:46.458
What was there for her to say? She had to go see Mr. Craven.

34
00:02:46.459 --> 00:02:50.163
Mrs. Medlock took her to a new part of the house.

35
00:02:50.164 --> 00:02:53.762
A man sat in an armchair near the fire.

36
00:02:53.763 --> 00:02:59.393
He was not so much a hunchback as a man with high, crooked shoulders.

37
00:02:59.394 --> 00:03:03.300
He dismissed Mrs. Medlock before he spoke to Mary.

38
00:03:03.301 --> 00:03:07.854
"Are you well?" he asked. "Do they take good care of you?"

39
00:03:07.855 --> 00:03:10.902
"Yes," she answered.

40
00:03:10.903 --> 00:03:14.862
His black eyes seemed as if they scarcely saw her.

41
00:03:14.863 --> 00:03:17.963
His black hair was streaked with white.

42
00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:21.984
He would have been handsome if he had not looked so miserable.

43
00:03:21.985 --> 00:03:25.627
"I forgot about you," said Mr. Craven.

44
00:03:25.628 --> 00:03:30.041
"I meant to send you a nurse or a governess."

45
00:03:30.042 --> 00:03:35.726
"Please . . ." Mary could hardly speak because of the lump in her throat.

46
00:03:35.727 --> 00:03:41.389
"Please . . . I'm too old for a nurse . . . and I don't need a governess."

47
00:03:41.390 --> 00:03:45.916
"That's what that Sowerby woman said," he muttered to himself.

48
00:03:45.917 --> 00:03:51.707
"Is that Martha's mother? She knows all about children. She has 12."

49
00:03:51.708 --> 00:03:53.669
"What do you want to do?"

50
00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:59.024
"I want to play outdoors. It makes me hungry, and I'm getting stronger."

51
00:03:59.025 --> 00:04:04.312
Mary tried to sound brave. "I run and skip everywhere."

52
00:04:04.313 --> 00:04:07.681
"Don't look so frightened. You may do what you like.

53
00:04:07.682 --> 00:04:11.875
Do you want toys, books, dolls?"

54
00:04:11.876 --> 00:04:14.310
"Might I have a bit of dirt?"

55
00:04:14.311 --> 00:04:19.202
Mr. Craven looked startled at this strange request. "Dirt?"

56
00:04:19.203 --> 00:04:22.627
"To plant seeds in, to watch the plants grow.

57
00:04:22.628 --> 00:04:25.665
I didn't really know about gardens in India.

58
00:04:25.666 --> 00:04:30.842
I sometimes played at sticking flowers in the ground, but here it's different."

59
00:04:30.843 --> 00:04:35.972
Mr. Craven got up and began to walk slowly around the room.

60
00:04:35.973 --> 00:04:41.206
When he stopped and looked at her, his eyes seemed almost kind.

61
00:04:41.207 --> 00:04:44.385
"You may have as much dirt as you want.

62
00:04:44.386 --> 00:04:48.784
You remind me of someone else who loved the earth and things that grow.

63
00:04:48.785 --> 00:04:56.366
When you see a bit of dirt you want"—and here he almost smiled—"take it, child, and make it come alive.

64
00:04:56.367 --> 00:04:59.325
Now you must go."

65
00:04:59.326 --> 00:05:05.523
He summoned Mrs. Medlock, who led Mary down the corridors and left her at her rooms.

66
00:05:05.524 --> 00:05:10.933
"I can have my garden!" Mary said to herself as she ran outside.

67
00:05:10.934 --> 00:05:15.731
When she opened the door to the secret garden, Dickon was gone.

68
00:05:15.732 --> 00:05:25.126
But she found a note: a picture of a bird on a nest with the words "I will come back."

